    "description": "Advanced Cooling Technologies (ACT) designs and manufactures thermal-management components and systems, including two-phase cooling, heat pipes, phase-change materials, cold plates and environmental-control units. The Lancaster, Pennsylvania-based platform serves data centers, advanced computing, defense, space, electronics, medical, industrial and HVAC markets, with additional integrated operations in York, Pennsylvania and Anaheim, California. Blackstone Energy Transition Partners announced a majority investment on March 11, 2026 and the transaction closed on May 19, 2026 through BETP IV; the exact percentage and management rollover are not publicly disclosed. ACT announced more than $5 million of additional capacity investment, a planned 50,000-square-foot facility and up to 100 new jobs in July 2026. No later sale, transfer or signed pending ownership transaction was identified through August 23, 2026.",
